{"id":"pamir-highway","title":"Pamir Highway (M41)","who":"Classic overland route","when":"Best from June to September","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycles, bicycles and 4x4s","kind":"moto","color":"#7c2d12","summary":"About 1,200 km across the \"Roof of the World\" from Osh in Kyrgyzstan to Dushanbe in Tajikistan, over passes above 4,600 m, past high lakes and along the Afghan border on the Panj river. One of the great overland roads.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Pamir Highway","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pamir_Highway"}],"approximate":"Main places on the road; the line between them is approximate. Permits (GBAO) are needed.","km":1269,"bbox":[68.7865,37.4856,74.0479,40.5464],"stops":[{"name":"Osh","place":"Osh, Kyrgyzstan","at":[40.5173,72.805],"text":"An ancient Silk Road town and the usual start.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Osh_03-2016_img27_view_from_Sulayman_Mountain.jpg/500px-Osh_03-2016_img27_view_from_Sulayman_Mountain.jpg","page":"Osh","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osh_03-2016_img27_view_from_Sulayman_Mountain.jpg","credit":"A.Savin","license":"FAL"}},{"name":"Sary-Tash","place":"Sary-Tash","at":[39.73,73.25],"text":"The Alay valley with the Pamir wall rising ahead."},{"name":"Karakul","place":"Karakul","at":[39.02,73.55],"text":"Over the Kyzyl-Art pass to a huge lake at almost 4,000 m.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Kara-kul_lake.jpg/500px-Kara-kul_lake.jpg","page":"Karakul (Tajikistan)","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kara-kul_lake.jpg","credit":"NASA","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Murghab","place":"Murghab","at":[38.17,73.96],"text":"Over Ak-Baital, at about 4,650 m the highest pass, to a high-plateau town.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Murghab_east_entry.jpg/500px-Murghab_east_entry.jpg","page":"Murghob","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murghab_east_entry.jpg","credit":"Kondephy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Khorog","place":"Khorog, Tajikistan","at":[37.4909,71.5489],"text":"Down to the Panj river and the Afghan border.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Khorog_1.jpg/500px-Khorog_1.jpg","page":"Khorog","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khorog_1.jpg","credit":"Troetona","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"The Panj valley","place":"Rushan, Tajikistan","at":[37.9416,71.5736],"text":"Afghanistan just across the river, close enough to wave."},{"name":"Kalai-Khumb","place":"Qalai Khumb, Tajikistan","at":[38.4541,70.7886],"text":"Rough road through deep gorges."},{"name":"Dushanbe","place":"Dushanbe, Tajikistan","at":[38.5767,68.7854],"text":"Tajikistan's capital, and the end of the highway.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Panorama_with_buildings%2C_Dushanbe.jpg/500px-Panorama_with_buildings%2C_Dushanbe.jpg","page":"Dushanbe","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_with_buildings%2C_Dushanbe.jpg","credit":"Adam Harangozó","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":187,"line":[[40.5174,72.8053],[40.5343,72.808],[40.5464,72.9168],[40.511,72.975],[40.5134,73.0234],[40.3739,73.1197],[40.2446,73.3207],[40.2533,73.4075],[40.3063,73.44],[40.297,73.4728],[40.2577,73.49],[40.2247,73.472],[40.1842,73.4852],[40.1709,73.5104],[40.1349,73.514],[40.1067,73.5429],[40.0487,73.5416],[40.0256,73.4943],[39.979,73.4944],[39.8998,73.4216],[39.8561,73.3456],[39.8383,73.2764],[39.773,73.2044],[39.7736,73.174],[39.7501,73.1507],[39.73,73.25]]},{"by":"ride","km":99,"line":[[39.73,73.25],[39.7048,73.2289],[39.5203,73.2699],[39.4319,73.2491],[39.3798,73.3291],[39.3085,73.3374],[39.1707,73.4738],[39.1251,73.5692],[39.0588,73.5973],[39.0151,73.554]]},{"by":"ride","km":134,"line":[[39.0151,73.554],[38.8128,73.453],[38.6834,73.5309],[38.6414,73.5259],[38.5753,73.546],[38.5603,73.5877],[38.5758,73.6547],[38.569,73